@prefix :       <http://example.org/philosophy#> .
@prefix owl:    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms:<http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix foaf:   <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/> .
@prefix crm:    <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/> .
@prefix wd:     <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/> .
@prefix dbr:    <http://dbpedia.org/resource/> .

###############################################################################
#  LINKED OPEN DATA LAYER
#
#  Implements Linked Data Principle 4 from Week 9, Lecture 9: "Include links
#  to other URIs, so that they can discover more things." The lecture
#  distinguishes three kinds of outbound link, and all three appear below:
#
#    * Identity links    -> owl:sameAs to Wikidata and DBpedia
#    * Vocabulary links  -> alignment to FOAF, SKOS, Dublin Core, CIDOC-CRM
#    * Relationship links-> rdfs:seeAlso to the authority record
#
#  PROVENANCE. Every Wikidata QID below was resolved programmatically against
#  the live Wikidata API on 2026-11-21 and then VERIFIED, not merely matched
#  by label:
#    - Philosophers (31/31): candidate items filtered to instance-of human
#      (P31=Q5), then confirmed by comparing birth year (P569) with the
#      birthYear asserted in philosophy_dataset.ttl, allowing the one-year
#      BCE offset between historical and ISO-8601 astronomical numbering.
#    - Works (30/30): candidate items confirmed by author (P50) pointing at
#      the already-verified QID of the work's :createdBy philosopher.
#  Label search alone was NOT trusted: it returns "capital city" for
#  Capital and "medical ethics" for Ethics. Where several items shared a
#  label, the one carrying an en.wikipedia sitelink was preferred, because
#  the others are individual editions and translations rather than the work.
#
#  DBpedia IRIs are derived from the en.wikipedia sitelink, which is exactly
#  how DBpedia mints its resource IRIs. Three works have no en.wikipedia
#  article, so they carry a Wikidata link only.
###############################################################################

###############################################################################
#  1. VOCABULARY LINKS - align local classes with standard vocabularies
#
#  Reusing established vocabulary rather than minting everything locally is
#  the core Linked Data practice (Heath & Bizer 2011, Sec. 4.4.4). The
#  alignments are deliberately rdfs:subClassOf / subPropertyOf rather than
#  owl:equivalentClass: our classes are NARROWER than the external ones
#  (every :Philosopher is a foaf:Person, but not conversely).
###############################################################################

:Philosopher     rdfs:subClassOf foaf:Person , crm:E21_Person .
:Work            rdfs:subClassOf crm:E73_Information_Object .
:Location        rdfs:subClassOf crm:E53_Place .
:TimePeriod      rdfs:subClassOf crm:E4_Period .
:Engagement      rdfs:subClassOf crm:E7_Activity .
:Concept         rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept .
:SchoolOfThought rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept .
:Reader          rdfs:subClassOf foaf:Person .

# Property alignments.
:title         rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:title .
:createdBy     rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:creator .
:references    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:references .
:subSchoolOf   rdfs:subPropertyOf skos:broader .
:createdIn     rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:spatial .
:composedDuring rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:temporal .

